# Multi-Department Staff Assignment (Session Context)

Enable staff members (e.g., float managers, nursing supervisors) to be authorized for multiple departments and select which department they are covering at login time. This replaces the current 1:1 user→department relationship with a many-to-many model + session-based department selection.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Breaking Change to `users.department_id`**: The existing `department_id` column on the `users` table will be retained as the **"primary/home department"** (backward-compatible), but it will no longer be the sole source of truth for authorization. A new `user_departments` junction table becomes the authoritative source.

> [!WARNING]
> **JWT Claims Impact**: The `department_id` claim currently baked into the JWT (used by RLS policies) will need to be set dynamically at login time based on the department the user selects. This requires updating how `app_metadata.department_id` is set during session establishment.

